  "description": "PLEASE NOTE: ALL ENQUIRIES BY EMAIL ONLY\n\nKelly Bradshaw are delighted to bring to the rental market in Crescent House — a beautifully efficient one-bedroom first floor apartment, perfectly designed for easy, low-maintenance living. Tucked within an attractive period building surrounded by mature gardens, this home proves that a smaller footprint doesn't mean compromising on charm, comfort, or location. With the added bonus of a parking space — a genuinely handy feature for city living — this apartment offers everything you need without anything you don't. \n\nThe accommodation comprises a welcoming hallway with guest closet, a well-proportioned living room with feature marble fireplace, a separate fitted kitchen, one comfortable bedroom, and a bathroom with shower.\n\nAdd to that a dedicated parking space, something that's become genuinely hard to find for city-centre-adjacent living, and this apartment offers a rare combination of convenience and character.\n\nThe Crescent is one of Dublin 3's most attractive residential addresses — a quiet, tree-lined setting with genuine period character. Crescent House sits within its own well-tended communal gardens, with a secure intercom entry system to the front gates, offering a real sense of calm and security rarely found this close to the city. Fairview Park and Clontarf seafront are both close by, and the DART at Clontarf Road, along with regular bus routes, puts the city centre within easy reach. For anyone who drives, having your own parking space just steps from your door is a real luxury this close in.\n\n\n\n",
